## Requests

Failures that can succeed on a second try (408, 409, 429, 5xx, dropped connections) are retried
with exponential backoff, honouring `Retry-After`; `max_retries=2` by default. Errors are
`{{ c.pkg }}.APIError` subclasses whose message says how to fix the problem.

Every method accepts per-request options as keyword arguments:

```python
client.{{ c.resources[0].module }}.{{ "list" }}(
    timeout=10, max_retries=0, extra_headers={"X-Debug": "1"}, extra_query={"a": "b"}, extra_body={"c": "d"},
)
```

Leave an optional argument out to send nothing; pass `None` to send `null`. Unknown enum values
and union variants are kept rather than rejected.
{% if c.idempotency_header %}

Every non-GET request gets a fresh `{{ c.idempotency_header }}`, reused by its retries. Pass
`idempotency_key="..."` to choose your own.
{% endif %}

`client.with_raw_response.<resource>.<method>(...)` returns the status, headers and parsed body:

```python
response = client.with_raw_response.{{ c.resources[0].module }}.{{ "list" }}()
print(response.status_code, response.headers["x-request-id"], response.parsed)
```

Set `{{ c.env_log }}=debug` to log requests, with credentials redacted.

## Pagination, streaming and files

List methods return a page. Iterate it to walk every item, or use `page.items`,
`page.has_next_page()` and `page.next_page()`.

Event-stream methods return a stream; close it early with `with` or `.close()`. Downloads return
`bytes`; the `*_to_file(dest, ...)` variant streams them to disk. Uploads take bytes, a path or an
open file.
